istance_km":22.9,"bearing_deg":118.2,"in_corridor":false,"resolution":"outside the corridor (22.9 km, 41° off the wind)"},{"incident":"425347","entity":"INEOS Americas Pasadena Site","rn":"RN100213958","start_local":"2024-06-21T09:38","compound":"Benzene","pounds":7634.0,"facility_id":"110000462623","distance_km":10.6,"bearing_deg":75.6,"in_corridor":true,"resolution":"in the upwind corridor"}],"ongoing_incidents":[],"search_scope":"Searched every STEERS emissions event starting 06/21/2024 in Harris County (2 found; search complete). Also searched reports that started in the 30 days before and were still running (0 open that day; earlier search complete).","status":"reported","incident":"425347","matched_facility_id":"110000462623","source_url":"https://www2.tceq.texas.gov/oce/eer/index.cfm?fuseaction=main.getDetails&target=425347","checks":[{"at":"T+24h","status":"reported","note":"initial notice filed 2024-06-21T14:38 local, 5.0 h after the reported discovery 2024-06-21T09:38"},{"at":"T+14d","status":"reported","note":"final report dated 2024-07-03, 12 days after the event ended"}],"compound_match":true,"reported":{"facility":"INEOS Americas Pasadena Site","compound":"Benzene","pounds":7634.0,"start_local":"2024-06-21T09:38","end_local":"2024-06-21T10:42","tz":"local (CDT)","cause":"Pump, P-2, experienced a mechanical failure when its seal blew causing benzene to release","match_basis":"started near the spike","revisions":[{"date":"2024-12-11","text":"The Basis Used to Determine Quantities field states 24,476 lbs. of vapor emissions and that should also be 7,634 pounds."}],"travel_h":0.97,"travel_speed_mph":6.8,"travel_distance_km":10.6,"start_to_spike_h":0.37,"arrival_local":"2024-06-21T10:36","spike_hour_local":["2024-06-21T10:00","2024-06-21T11:00"]}},"corridor":{"origin_site_id":"48_201_0069","half_width_deg":22.5,"max_km":15.0,"wind_from_deg":[57.0,77.0]},"packet":{"draft_en":"On June 21, 2024, the Texas state monitor at Houston Milby Park recorded 51.75 ppb of benzene in the 9:00 a.m. CST hour, against a 7-day median of 0.21 ppb. Manchester East Ave N recorded 21.4 ppb in the same hour. Wind there came from 77 degrees at 6.8 mph. 47 major permitted facilities lie in the upwind corridor. One of them, INEOS Americas Pasadena Site, filed emissions-event report 425347 for 7,634 pounds of benzene from 09:38 to 10:42 local time that day. The reported release window and the wind line up with these readings; other sources may also contribute. Requested follow-up: confirm whether nearby residents were notified, and whether the reported amount accounts for these readings.","draft_es":"El 21 de junio de 2024, el monitor estatal de Texas en Houston Milby Park registró 51.75 ppb de benceno en la hora de las 9:00 a. m. CST, frente a una mediana de 7 días de 0.21 ppb. Manchester East Ave N registró 21.4 ppb en la misma hora. El viento venía de 77 grados a 6.8 mph. Hay 47 instalaciones grandes con permiso en el corredor viento arriba. Una de ellas, INEOS Americas Pasadena Site, presentó el reporte de evento de emisiones 425347 por 7,634 libras de benceno de 09:38 a 10:42, hora local, ese día. El horario de la emisión reportada y el viento coinciden con estas lecturas; otras fuentes también pueden contribuir. Seguimiento solicitado: confirmar si se avisó a los residentes cercanos y si la cantidad reportada explica estas lecturas.","drafted_by":"template (deterministic, no AI)","guard":{"passed":true,"rejected":[]}},"cannot_say":["A matching report is not proof the facility caused every reading; other sources can add to a spike.","'Not yet reported' is not a finding about any facility: Texas requires a report only at or above a reportable quantity, and air readings cannot measure how much was released (30 TAC 101.201).","The upwind corridor comes from wind direction at one monitor (geometry only), not a dispersion model; it cannot tell facilities along the same bearing apart.","Facility coordinates are as published by EPA ECHO and may b